&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;[Full-time] • Remote&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Boldin, we believe financial confidence should be accessible to everyone. Money decisions shape our lives, yet too often people are left without the clarity or tools they need to make informed choices. We exist to change that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Boldin is a comprehensive financial planning platform that helps people understand their financial picture, make smarter decisions with their money and time, and plan for the future with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With over $20M raised and strong momentum, Boldin is entering a pivotal phase of growth. This is an opportunity to join a mission-driven team and help shape the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Boldin helps people plan for and live a confident retirement. The &lt;strong&gt;Time to Value (TTV)&lt;/strong&gt; team owns the top of the funnel — the experience from a visitor&#39;s first touch through registration, onboarding, account linking, trial, and conversion to a paying subscriber. It&#39;s where prospective members decide whether Boldin is worth their trust, so the work is equal parts product polish and reliable, integration-heavy engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Full Stack Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to strengthen this team. Much of the funnel runs on third-party integrations — payment platforms, financial account aggregation, lifecycle messaging, and analytics — and we need someone who is comfortable owning that connective tissue end-to-end, from a React/TypeScript front end through a Ruby on Rails back end to the webhooks that tie external services together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the registration, onboarding, checkout, and conversion flows that move visitors to activated, paying members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own integrations across the funnel: payment platforms, lifecycle/marketing messaging, and product analytics — including the webhook handlers and gateway services that keep them in sync.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the ongoing &lt;strong&gt;payments migration&lt;/strong&gt; (consolidating multiple legacy payment platforms onto our primary processor) and help simplify a multi-gateway billing setup.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the stack: React/TypeScript on the front end, Ruby on Rails on the back end, with the data and webhook plumbing in between.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, and the broader engineering org to instrument and improve top-of-funnel conversion, grounded in analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write tested, maintainable code and participate in code review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll work on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The funnel touches a broad set of external systems. You won&#39;t need experience with all of them, but this is the landscape:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payments &amp;amp; billing:&lt;/strong&gt; multiple platforms today (primary processor plus legacy gateways and cart/checkout tools), with an active migration to consolidate them. Subscription lifecycle, webhooks, and tax handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial-account aggregation:&lt;/strong&gt; linking members&#39; real financial accounts during onboarding — a core, trust-critical part of the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lifecycle &amp;amp; support messaging:&lt;/strong&gt; in-app messaging/support, marketing automation, and transactional email.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytics &amp;amp; experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt; product analytics and a customer-data pipeline used to measure and improve funnel conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KPIS + Targets&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trial Cancels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subscriber Churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder NPS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integration cost efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of professional software engineering experience, &lt;strong&gt;primarily backend&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with a &lt;strong&gt;server-side framework and relational database&lt;/strong&gt; (we use Ruby on Rails; comparable experience is fine if you&#39;re eager to pick up Rails).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building &lt;strong&gt;webhook-driven, third-party API integrations&lt;/strong&gt;, with sound reasoning about failure, retries, and idempotency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working proficiency&lt;/strong&gt; with a modern JS/TypeScript front-end framework (we use React) — comfortable contributing to the front end when the work calls for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic eye for the user experience, especially in high-stakes flows like signup and payment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong plus&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;financial-account aggregation&lt;/strong&gt; providers (Plaid, Finicity, Yodlee, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ruby on Rails experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience migrating or consolidating payment/billing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in fintech, financial services, or another domain with sensitive user data and compliance considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with CRM, lifecycle, or analytics tooling (Intercom, ActiveCampaign, Segment, or similar) — these are learnable on the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience optimizing top-of-funnel conversion and running experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our stack&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Front end:&lt;/strong&gt; React, TypeScript, Material-UI, Redux, SWR (Yarn workspaces monorepo)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Back end:&lt;/strong&gt; Ruby on Rails, PostgreSQL, Sidekiq&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrations:&lt;/strong&gt; Stripe, Braintree, ChargeDesk, Plaid, Intercom, Segment, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infra &amp;amp; data:&lt;/strong&gt; AWS, plus a data pipeline for analytics&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Salary Range&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$160,000 - 195,000 DOE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to be as inclusive as possible in our hiring process. If you don’t have 100% of what we’re looking for, but feel like you’re pretty close to growing into the role — please still apply. If a candidate has only 80% of the skills but a fantastic attitude and perspective, they might be the perfect fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Boldin values the unique perspectives and contributions of all individuals and we strive to foster a diverse and inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, including and not limited to people of any race, ethnicity, or national origin, individuals with differing abilities, members of the LGBTQ+ community, veterans, gender minorities, women and people from underrepresented communities.We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations for applicants with differing abilities throughout the recruitment process. If you require any accommodations, please let us know, and we will work with you to meet your needs. We are committed to fostering an environment where everyone can bring their authentic selves to work. If you are comfortable doing so we invite you to share your preferred pronouns in your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Designer · Contract&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;3 months, extendable • ~ 25-30 hours/week • Remote&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Boldin helps anyone build a comprehensive financial plan and understand how today&#39;s decisions shape their future. We&#39;ve recently raised $20M+ from top investors, seen exponential growth, and are scaling the team to meet the moment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;About This Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a &lt;strong&gt;contract Marketing Designer&lt;/strong&gt; to give Boldin&#39;s marketing team dedicated design support over the next quarter: campaign creative, landing pages, lifecycle email, paid social, and event materials, shipped at the pace a growth team moves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a production-focused role. You&#39;ll work inside Boldin&#39;s brand guidelines and templates, partner directly with marketing on concepts and variants, and report to design leadership. Your job is to make sure marketing never waits on design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll work on&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Landing pages and web campaign assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lifecycle and marketing emails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Presentations and sales/partner decks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid and organic social creative, including A/B variants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conference, webinar, and event materials (digital and print)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Graphics and assets for the video team to use in motion work (motion design itself not required)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Templates for recurring formats so marketing can self-serve common assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Final production files, specs, and handoff to marketing and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own day-to-day design execution for marketing requests from brief through final files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring ideas to growth, lifecycle, content, and events, not just execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build creative in variants and adjust based on results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the video team with graphics, frames, and assets for motion pieces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Boldin&#39;s brand guidelines, templates, and component libraries as the source of truth; escalate anything the system can&#39;t answer to design leadership rather than inventing around it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn repeat requests into templates so the next version takes a fraction of the time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep files organized and documented so work can be handed to the incoming full-time designer without loss.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of marketing or brand design experience, with in-house or agency work for product companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio showing volume and range across web, email, presentations, digital advertising, and print, with strong fundamentals in typography, layout, and color&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work fast within an established brand system and keep quality high at pace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert in Figma, including components, variables, and shared libraries; this is where all of our design work lives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building templates others used to produce assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working directly with marketers and taking direction from design leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performance-driven creative (variants, tests, iteration)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motion design is a plus, not a requirement; experience preparing assets for video or motion teams is&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI in your production workflow is a plus, not a requirement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available to start within two weeks&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;$60 - $80/ Hour DOE&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to be as inclusive as possible in our hiring process. If you don’t have 100% of what we’re looking for, but feel like you’re pretty close to growing into the role — please still apply. If a candidate has only 80% of the skills but a fantastic attitude and perspective, they might be the perfect fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Boldin values the unique perspectives and contributions of all individuals and we strive to foster a diverse and inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, including and not limited to people of any race, ethnicity, or national origin, individuals with differing abilities, members of the LGBTQ+ community, veterans, gender minorities, women and people from underrepresented communities.We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations for applicants with differing abilities throughout the recruitment process. If you require any accommodations, please let us know, and we will work with you to meet your needs. We are committed to fostering an environment where everyone can bring their authentic selves to work. If you are comfortable doing so we invite you to share your preferred pronouns in your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;[Full-time] • Remote&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Boldin, we believe financial confidence should be accessible to everyone. Money decisions shape our lives, yet too often people are left without the clarity or tools they need to make informed choices. We exist to change that.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Boldin is a comprehensive financial planning platform that helps people understand their financial picture, make smarter decisions with their money and time, and plan for the future with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With over $20M raised and strong momentum, Boldin is entering a pivotal phase of growth. This is an opportunity to join a mission-driven team and help shape the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Performance Marketing Lead&lt;/strong&gt; to own paid user acquisition end to end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll own the paid budget, the channel mix, and the number. Today, that means search and paid social do the heavy lifting; from there, you&#39;ll decide where we expand next—CTV, podcast, and paid sponsorships, or somewhere we haven&#39;t tried yet. You&#39;ll make that call based on what the data says, not what&#39;s fashionable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role with real scope. You&#39;ll be in the accounts, writing copy, setting up landing page tests, reporting out on the numbers, and hitting our CAC targets. You&#39;ll work directly with our Head of Growth, and closely with data, product, lifecycle, and creative partners. If you like to be hands-on while driving the strategy, this is a good fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own paid acquisition strategy and execution across all paid channels, with an initial focus on SEM and paid social, then expanding into CTV, paid sponsorships, and new channels as the data supports it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the paid media budget: allocation across channels, pacing, and reallocation away from non efficient spend toward what&#39;s working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run end-to-end campaign management—strategy, build, launch, optimization, analysis, and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize account performance through ongoing keyword work, ad copy testing, campaign structure improvements, and bid strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a consistent testing cadence across ad copy, creative formats, audiences, targeting, and landing pages, and turn results into a documented learning loop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and design to improve landing page and funnel conversion rates, bringing specific recommendations rather than general feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage performance against efficiency targets (CAC, LTV:CAC, CPA, ROAS) rather than top-of-funnel volume alone, and connect paid spend to registrations, trial starts, and new customer revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze audience and placement data to find new opportunities and cut inefficient segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on paid performance and test results weekly, and translate results into a clear point of view on what we do next&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our data team to make sure attribution, tracking, and conversion measurement are trustworthy—and flag it loudly when they aren&#39;t&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and manage agencies, vendors, and tools where they extend our capacity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the acquisition roadmap based on performance, seasonality, competitive shifts, and new audience insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years in performance marketing or paid acquisition, with meaningful time in a consumer/B2C environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on operator experience in Google Ads and paid social (Meta at minimum; Reddit, LinkedIn, YouTube, or TikTok a plus)—you&#39;ve built and optimized accounts yourself, not just briefed an agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of owning a paid budget of at least $1M annually and hitting efficiency targets, with specific numbers you can walk through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills: comfortable pulling your own numbers from BI or warehouse layer, and able to build your own reporting rather than waiting on someone else&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of attribution, incrementality, and measurement limitations—you know when a number is directional vs. reliable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with subscription or freemium business models, and comfort optimizing to downstream revenue rather than lead volume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated CRO instincts and experience partnering on landing page and funnel testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication—you can explain performance and tradeoffs to a leadership audience without a translator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating in a small, fast-moving team where you set your own priorities&lt;br&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Salary Range&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;4,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;49&quot;&gt;$140,000 – $175,000&lt;/strong&gt; + Equity + Performance Based Bonus - DOE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We want to be as inclusive as possible in our hiring process. If you don’t have 100% of what we’re looking for, but feel like you’re pretty close to growing into the role — please still apply. If a candidate has only 80% of the skills but a fantastic attitude and perspective, they might be the perfect fit.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Boldin values the unique perspectives and contributions of all individuals and we strive to foster a diverse and inclusive culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, including and not limited to people of any race, ethnicity, or national origin, individuals with differing abilities, members of the LGBTQ+ community, veterans, gender minorities, women and people from underrepresented communities.We are committed to providing reasonable accommodations for applicants with differing abilities throughout the recruitment process. If you require any accommodations, please let us know, and we will work with you to meet your needs. We are committed to fostering an environment where everyone can bring their authentic selves to work. If you are comfortable doing so we invite you to share your preferred pronouns in your application. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Brand Designer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(4, 180, 119);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Time • Remote&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Boldin helps anyone build a comprehensive financial plan and understand how today&#39;s decisions shape their future. We&#39;ve recently raised $20M+ from top investors, seen exponential growth, and are scaling the team to meet the moment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;About This Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Brand Designer&lt;/strong&gt; to own how Boldin shows up in the world — from first impression to everyday use of the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Financial planning is emotional, high-stakes, and historically cold. Your job is to build a brand that makes it feel human, leaving people confident, informed, and empowered to make great financial decisions. You&#39;ll own the evolution and vision of Boldin&#39;s visual expression across every touchpoint, from marketing to product, from social to motion, while working directly with founders and leadership to shape where the brand goes next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for a designer who builds systems, not just assets. You&#39;ll create the workflows, templates, and AI-driven pipelines that keep every generated asset unmistakably Boldin — so the whole company can move fast without the brand fracturing. You&#39;ll also raise the bar for craft and brand story in everything we ship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll do well here if you care deeply about helping people make better financial decisions, you operate with high agency, and are energized by a startup environment where you&#39;ll wear many hats and own outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the brand vision: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead the evolution of Boldin&#39;s visual identity and brand story across every touchpoint, from web and social to product and motion, partnering with founders and leadership to shape the brand&#39;s future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the brand engine:&lt;/strong&gt; Create and maintain the workflows, tools, and templates that keep generated brand assets consistent at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fuel marketing:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the marketing team on creative directions, campaigns, and end deliverables while testing to optimize outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge product &amp;amp; brand: &lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with the product team to create one cohesive brand experience across the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Co-own design systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Co-create and maintain Boldin&#39;s brand and product design systems, optimizing both for human and AI-driven workflows to produce on-brand work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate with AI:&lt;/strong&gt; Embrace new technology to move faster on production and exploration, while pushing past generic AI output with taste, judgment, and critical thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the bar:&lt;/strong&gt; Empathize deeply with our customers and obsess over how the Boldin brand is expressed in every detail we ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;Qualifications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of brand design experience, including meaningful in-house work at product companies (fintech or other trust-heavy domains a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio showing exceptional craft across typography, layout, color, and motion, including brand systems you built, scaled, or evolved&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a brand&#39;s creative direction, including at least one rebrand or brand evolution you led from concept through rollout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active use of AI in your creative workflow, from ideation to production pipelines, with shipped work and a clear point of view on where AI accelerates and where human judgment matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outcomes driven: comfortable tying creative work to marketing tests and business results, and adjusting based on what you learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering directly with founders, executives, and cross-functional teams in a fast-moving startup environment&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 63, 74);&quot;&gt;Salary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;4,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;49&quot;&gt;$160,000 – $180,000&lt;/strong&gt; + Equity + Performance Based Bonus - DOE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We want to be as inclusive as possible in our hiring process. If you don’t have 100% of what we’re looking for, but feel like you’re pretty close to growing into the role — please still apply. If a candidate has only 80% of the skills but a fantastic attitude and perspective, they might be the perfect fit.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
